## Why This Is Asked

This ensures scalable, fair CKNE-driven caching across many tenants, balancing latency and hit rate in real time.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-to-quota mapping with a guaranteed baseline
- CKNE-aware eviction policy (weighted LFU/LRU) plus selective prefetch
- Minute-by-minute rebalancing with safety guards and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
function computeQuotas(totSlots, tenants){
  const total = tenants.reduce((s,t)=>s+t.ckne,0);
  return tenants.map(t=>{
    const w = Math.max(0.05, t.ckne);
    const q = Math.max(1, Math.round((w/total)*totSlots));
    return {tenant: t.tenant, quota: q};
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle sudden CKNE spikes or missing data?
- What metrics confirm SLA while maintaining fairness?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests CKNE-aware scheduling for ML inference in a multi-tenant GPU cluster, focusing on real-time dynamics, SLA guarantees, and fairness.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE to per-tenant resource mapping (concurrency, batch, memory)
- minute-by-minute rebalancing with SLA guarantees
- per-tenant quotas and fairness under traffic spikes

## Code Example
```javascript
function mapCKNE(ckne){
  const concurrency = Math.max(1, Math.min(8, Math.round(2 + ckne * 6)));
  const batch = Math.max(1, Math.min(128, Math.round(16 + ckne * 112)));
  const memMB = Math.round(256 + ckne * 1024);
  return {concurrency, batch, memMB};
}
```

